<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  THE camera mounting pose. Single source of truth, included by both camera
  descriptions so sim and hardware cannot drift apart.

    rx150_gripper_depth_camera.urdf.xacro   sim, Gazebo depth sensor
    rx150_realsense_camera.urdf.xacro       hardware, RealSense driver

  Both bolt their camera link onto rx150/gripper_link with this pose, and both
  mean the same physical point - the camera's own reference origin, which for a
  D435 sits a few cm inside the casing. Measure to that point, not to the
  casing, or fold the casing offset in here.

  xyz is MEASURED. rpy is NOT; see the warning at the bottom.

  ===========================================================================
  Where xyz comes from
  ===========================================================================
  Measured by hand from the green dot (mount_ref_corner in
  rx150_gripper_depth_camera.urdf.xacro) to the DEPTH camera origin, which is
  the point camera_link names and the point this file must land on.

  The raw measurement was taken in a different frame from gripper_link, so it
  is transformed here rather than copied. Do not paste new numbers in without
  redoing this: the axes do not line up, and nothing errors if they are wrong.

    measured frame                      gripper_link (REP-103)
      x = across the gripper,             y = LEFT     (negated)
          +x toward the RIGHT
      y = height, +y up                   z = up       (as is)
      z = out along the view              x = forward  (as is)

    raw (mm)             x -1.930    y +26.525   z +37.660
    in gripper_link axes x +37.660   y +1.930    z +26.525
    green dot (m)        [0.03700, 0.01425, 0.02925]
    dot + offset         [0.07466, 0.01618, 0.05577]

  The dot is itself estimated to a few mm (the sim mesh has no screw holes), so
  treat the last digit as decoration, not precision.

  ===========================================================================
  rpy IS STILL UNMEASURED
  ===========================================================================
  0 0 0 asserts the camera is mounted perfectly square to the gripper. Nobody
  has checked that. It is the term that matters most for the obstacle map: a
  rotation error does not shift the map, it SMEARS it, because each sweep
  station views the scene from a different angle and lands the same surface in
  a different place. 3 deg of pitch is about 26 mm of height error at 0.5 m,
  on its own enough to lift the work surface above the sweep's z_min crop and
  have the planner route around the table as if it were a wall.

  If the map still comes out thick with a correct xyz, measure this next.
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <xacro:property name="cam_mount_xyz" value="0.07466 0.01618 0.05577" scope="global"/>
  <xacro:property name="cam_mount_rpy" value="0 0 0"         scope="global"/>
</robot>
